WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.350
A library shelf, labelled: Classics.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.020
1847.

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.980
A passionate new novel arrives,
and startles its critics.

4
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.590
1899.

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.490
Another novel is mostly
attacked by reviewers,

6
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.360
and nearly vanishes.

7
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.860
Decades later, it's back,
with a gold sticker.

8
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.140
So who is moving the books?

9
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:23.770
Who decided which ones are classics?

10
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.610
In this mission, you'll
find out what a canon is,

11
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.800
and where the word first came from.

12
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.260
You'll weigh old arguments about
what makes a book valuable,

13
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.930
and test a poem that boasts
it will last for ever:

14
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.930
"Not marble, nor the gilded monuments".

15
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.610
And you'll track books whose
standing rose and fell.

16
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.940
Your mission: find out who
decided which books are classics.
